/T (The Art of Storytelling: A Timeless Tradition Since the dawn of civilization, storytelling has been an integral part of human culture. From cave paintings to oral traditions, communities have used stories to preserve their history, transmit values, and impart wisdom to future generations. Through the artful use of language, imagery, and emotion, storytellers have woven intricate tapestries of meaning that resonate deeply with audiences across time and space.)
